sappho:
You will not lie with my consent;
And Sappho is a roving dust;
Cressid could love again; Dido,

sapphire:
I saw his soul saw,—‘Jasper first,’ I said,
‘And second, sapphire; third, chalcedony;
The rest in order, ... last, an amethyst.’

saps:
Ice-bound, hunger-pinched and dim;
Dormant roots recall their saps,
Empty nests show black and grim,

sapless:
When the fog lifts.
Loosened from their sapless twigs
Leaves drop with every gust;

sappho's:
Helen of Troy had a wandering glance;
Sappho's restriction was only the sky;
Ninon was ever the chatter of France;

Wait, where older waters swell;
Ways that flowered at Sappho's tread,
Winds that sighed in Homer's strings,
